From 339688b422c818c9bce46b31e0dc026ddaedcaf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akapug <akapug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 19:50:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] speculative: the MTP drafter honours the per-sequence
 draft limit

The MTP draft loop stopped a sequence only at the global n_max and ignored the per-sequence
limit the caller sets in its draft params (the server derives it from the context space and
the tokens left to generate). It drafted up to n_max tokens for every sequence and the rest
were discarded or ran past the limit. Stop at either limit, as the simple drafter does.

With a server limit of 1 draft per slot and n_max 3 (Qwen3.8-27B, its own MTP head, Arc Pro
B70, 4 streams), decode went 80.0-80.6 -> 87.0-87.5 tok/s: each step no longer runs the MTP
head and the output head twice more per slot for drafts it throws away.
---
 common/speculative.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/speculative.cpp b/common/speculative.cpp
index 77dfe95..c0a924c 100644
--- a/common/speculative.cpp
+++ b/common/speculative.cpp
@@ -1697,7 +1697,7 @@ struct common_speculative_impl_draft_mtp : public common_speculative_impl {
 
                 result.push_back(id);
 
-                if (params.n_max <= (int) result.size()) {
+                if (params.n_max <= (int) result.size() || (dp.n_max > 0 && dp.n_max <= (int) result.size())) {
                     drafting[seq_id] = false;
                     n_drafting--;
                     continue;
